{"name":"Holy Ghost","hex":"#efe9e6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Holy Ghost","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The person (hypostasis) of the Trinity or Godhead corresponding to divine essence, which becomes present in and among the faithful (particularly inspired prophets) and is considered to proceed either  from God the Father alone or  from Him together with God the Son."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The plant Angelica archangelica."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Holy_Ghost"}],"entries":[{"title":"Holy Ghost (Modern Baseball album)","blocks":[{"text":"Holy Ghost is the third and final studio album by the American rock band Modern Baseball, released on May 13, 2016. The album follows their third EP, The Perfect Cast, which was released on October 23, 2015, via Lame-O Records, as well as their sophomore studio album, You're Gonna Miss It All, released in 2014, and their compilation album, Techniques, also released in 2014."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/07/Modernbaseballholyghost.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Ghost_(Modern_Baseball_album)"},{"title":"Holy Ghost (2025 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Holy Ghost is an American horror mystery film, released on 8 August 2025."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/82/Holy_Ghost_%282025_film%29_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Ghost_(2025_film)"},{"title":"Holy Spirit in Christianity","blocks":[{"text":"In mainstream Trinitarian Christianity, the Holy Spirit or Holy Ghost is the third Person of the Trinity, which is often enumerated as God the Father, God the Son, and God the Holy Spirit. Nontrinitarian Christians, who reject the doctrine of the Trinity, differ significantly from mainstream Christianity in their beliefs about the Holy Spirit. In Christian theology, pneumatology is the study of the Holy Spirit. Due to Christianity's historical relationship with Judaism, theologians often identify the Holy Spirit with the concept of the Ruach Hakodesh in Jewish scripture, on the theory that Jesus was expanding upon these Jewish concepts. Similar names, and ideas, include the Ruach Elohim and Ruach YHWH. In the New Testament the Holy Spirit is identified with the Spirit of Christ, the Spirit of Truth, and the Paraclete (helper)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Rom%2C_Vatikan%2C_Basilika_St._Peter%2C_Die_Taube_des_Heiligen_Geistes_%28Cathedra_Petri%2C_Bernini%29.jpg/330px-Rom%2C_Vatikan%2C_Basilika_St._Peter%2C_Die_Taube_des_Heiligen_Geistes_%28Cathedra_Petri%2C_Bernini%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Spirit_in_Christianity"},{"title":"Sacredness","blocks":[{"text":"Sacred describes something that is dedicated or set apart for the service or worship of a deity; is considered worthy of spiritual respect or devotion; or inspires awe or reverence among believers. The property is often ascribed to objects, or places."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacredness"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Philippe_de_Champaigne_-_Annunciation_-_WGA04705.jpg/500px-Philippe_de_Champaigne_-_Annunciation_-_WGA04705.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Philippe_de_Champaigne_-_Annunciation_-_WGA04705.jpg/500px-Philippe_de_Champaigne_-_Annunciation_-_WGA04705.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Holy Spirit as a dove in The Annunciation, by Philippe de Champaigne, 1644","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhilippe_de_Champaigne_-_Annunciation_-_WGA04705.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://